{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["And the width fifty by fifty — how so? The courtyard, its length is one hundred cubits from east to west, for the northern wall is one hundred cubits of hangings, and likewise the southern. And from north to south, fifty cubits is the width of the courtyard. And the Tabernacle, its length is thirty and its width ten. He placed the Tabernacle at the edge of fifty of the hundred, and there remained courtyard from the east in front of the Tabernacle fifty by fifty square, open; and on its three sides, courtyard of twenty cubits — for its length is thirty and there remained behind it to the west twenty of the fifty of the hundred-cubit length. And its width is ten, and there remained to the north side twenty of the fifty width, and likewise to the south side."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {0 "The bracketed phrase [המזרח לפני] in the source appears to be an editorial restoration; I translate it as integrated text."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:43:20.783234767Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}